   "source": [
    "two_electrode_circuit = schemdraw.Drawing(inches_per_unit=0.75)\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Dot(open=True).left())\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Line().left())\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Line().down())\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Line().right())\n",
    "\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Gap().label(''))\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Line().right())\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Line().up())\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Line().left())\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Dot(open=True).left())\n",
    "\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Gap().right().label(''))\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Gap().right().label(''))\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Dot(open=True))\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Resistor(label='Galvanic cell', fontsize=12))\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Dot(open=True))\n",
    "\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Gap().down().label(''))\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Dot(open=True))\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Battery(label='Electrolytic cell', fontsize=12).left())\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Dot(open=True))\n",
    "two_electrode_circuit.add(elm.Gap().down().label(''))\n",
    "\n",
    "# annotate diagram\n",
    "fig = two_electrode_circuit.draw()\n",
    "fig.plot([0, 0],[-2.5, -3.5]) # anode\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate('anode', (-0.75,-2.75))\n",
    "fig.plot([3, 3],[-2.5, -3.5]) # cathode\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate('cathode', (3.1,-2.75))\n",
    "fig.plot([1.5, 1.5],[-2, -4], ls=':', color='gray') # membrane\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate('separator membrane', (0.5, -1.75), color='gray')\n",
    "fig.plot([-1, -1, 4, 4, -1],[-2, -4, -4, -2, -2], fill=(0,0,1,0.05)) # reaction cell\n",
    "fig.ax.scatter([1],[-2.5], facecolor='none', edgecolor='red', marker='o', s=200) # cation\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate('cations', \n",
    "            xy=(1, -2.5), xycoords='data', \n",
    "            xytext=(2, -2.5), textcoords='data',\n",
    "            fontsize=10, arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='<-', color='red')\n",
    "               )\n",
    "fig.ax.scatter([2],[-3.5], facecolor='none', edgecolor='blue', marker='o', s=200) # anion\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate('anions', \n",
    "            xy=(2, -3.5), xycoords='data', \n",
    "            xytext=(0.5, -3.5), textcoords='data',\n",
    "            fontsize=10, arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='<-', color='blue')\n",
    "               )\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate(r'$A \\rightleftharpoons B + e^-$', (-3,-3.5), fontsize=12)\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate(r'$E^0_1, k_{1,a}, k_{1,c}$', (-3,-3.85), fontsize=12)\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate(r'$C + e^- \\rightleftharpoons D $', (4.5,-3.5), fontsize=12)\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate(r'$E^0_2, k_{2,a}, k_{2,c}$', (4.5,-3.85), fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "display(fig)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Some general characteristics of two electrode cells:\n",
    "- **Different half reactions** occur at each electrode surface, each with their own $E^0$, $k_a$ and $k_c$ values.\n",
    "- **Galvanic cells** can be used to power some electrical device\n",
    "- **Electrolytic cells** require the application of a voltage to pass charge\n",
    "- **Electrons** pass through an external circuit\n",
    "- **Ionic charge** must flow through the **electrolyte solution** to balance the movement of electronic charge\n",
    "- **Separator membranes** are often incorporated to inhibit unwanted reactions\n",
    "- Electrodes are termed **anode** or **cathode**, based on which reaction happens at their surface. This is traditionally assigned based on Galvanic operation of the cell (ie., the discharge of a battery)\n",
    "    - Battery terminology refers to the cathode as the \"positive\" electrode and the anode as the \"negative\" electrode"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Examples of two electrode cells include almost all commercial technologies:\n",
    "- **Batteries**: Li-ion, nickel metal hydride, redox flow, etc.\n",
    "- **Fuel cells**: H$_2$, methanol, formic acid, etc.\n",
    "- **Electrosynthesis cells**: H$_2$ & O$_2$, chlorate, chlor-alkali, adiponitrile, etc"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Primary advantage**: Simplicity!\n",
    "\n",
    "**Primary disadvantages**: One observes the overall behavior ($E^0_{rxn}$) rather than individual components ($E^0_1$ and $E^0_2$). This makes it difficult to identify, diagnose and study the co-existence of multiple reactions. Separation of electrodes yields solution resistance, which results in energy loss."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div class=\"alert alert-block alert-info\">\n",
    "<b>Activity:</b> Grab a pen and sketch a two-electrode cell for the reaction of your choice.\n",
    "<br>\n",
    "Label both electrodes, mark which way the electrons travel in the external circuit, and mark which way the cations travel in solution. Then say, in one sentence, what you would be able to measure and what you would <b>not</b>.\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Real world electrochemical cells with Canadian relevance**:\n",
    "- [Accelera: Previously \"Hydrogenics\", a leader in water electrolysis](https://www.accelerazero.com/)\n",
    "- [Hydrogen Optimized: Canadian company deploying water electrolyzers](https://hydrogenoptimized.com/)\n",
    "- [Ballard Power: Global leader in fuel cell technology](http://ballard.com/fuel-cell-solutions/fuel-cell-power-products/fuel-cell-stacks)\n",
    "- [Jacobs: Design and installation of industrial chlorate synthesis plants](https://darets.com/ets/workwithus/products/chemetics/index.html#SodiumChlorate)\n",
    "- [E-One Moli Energy: Lithium ion batteries](http://www.molicel.com/ca/products.html)\n",
    "- [NanoOne: Lithium ion batteries](https://nanoone.ca/)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Three Electrode Cells\n",
    "\n",
    "The addition of an extra electrode provides powerful new capabilities."
   ]
  },
